    {
      "answer_id": "A2",
      "answer": "Based on the provided context, the following genes are connected to the Hedgehog signaling pathway in the integrated graph:\n\n1. **SHH (Sonic hedgehog homologue)** \u2013 A key signaling molecule in the Hedgehog pathway, involved in the development of the male genital system and implicated in hypospadias. Its expression was found to be decreased in boys with proximal hypospadias.\n\n2. **PTCH1 (Protein patched homologue 1)** \u2013 A receptor for SHH, part of the Hedgehog signaling pathway. Its mRNA expression was significantly decreased in boys with proximal hypospadias.\n\n3. **GLI2 (Glioma-associated oncogene homologue 2)** \u2013 A transcription factor downstream of the Hedgehog pathway. Its mRNA expression was significantly decreased in both distal and proximal hypospadias.\n\n4. **SUFU (Suppressor of fused protein)** \u2013 A repressor of the Hedgehog pathway, involved in regulating the activity of Gli transcription factors. Its expression was not significantly different among the groups in the study.\n\n5. **SMO (Smoothened)** \u2013 A transmembrane protein that transmits the Hedgehog signal to the intracellular pathway. Its expression was not significantly different among the groups.\n\n6. **STK36 (Serine/threonine-protein kinase 36)** \u2013 A kinase involved in the phosphorylation of Ci/Gli proteins, which is part of the regulatory mechanism of the Hedgehog pathway. Its expression was not significantly different among the groups.\n\nThese genes are directly or indirectly involved in the Hedgehog signaling pathway, as described in the study."
